description:
Build a hosted form end-to-end from a single builder `document`: every field type, content blocks, conditional field visibility, theme styling, and welcome/ending screens. This is the FULL authoring path - prefer it over update_form when adding/replacing fields or styling. Requires `forms:write`.

The `document` mirrors what the visual builder saves:
{
  "builder": { "name": "Contact", "settings": {} },
  "blocks": [
    { "id": "blk_welcome", "kind": "welcome", "position": 0, "config": { "headline": "Get in touch", "body": "We reply within a day." } },
    { "id": "blk_q", "kind": "question", "position": 1, "elements": [
      { "type": "heading", "config": { "text": "Your details", "level": "h2" } },
      { "type": "open_text", "name": "full_name", "config": { "label": "Full name", "required": true } },
      { "type": "open_text", "name": "email", "config": { "label": "Email", "format": "email", "required": true } },
      { "type": "rating", "name": "satisfaction", "config": { "label": "How was it?" } },
      { "type": "range_slider", "name": "budget", "config": { "label": "Budget", "min": 0, "max": 1000, "step": 50 } }
    ] },
    { "id": "blk_end", "kind": "ending_screen", "position": 2, "config": { "headline": "Thanks!" } }
  ],
  "theme_v2": { "tokens": { "color": { "primary": "#0ea5e9" } } }
}

Element `type` vocabulary (input fields): open_text, multiple_choice_single, multiple_choice_multi, picture_selection, ranking, consent, file_upload, rating, nps, matrix, contact_info, cta, stripe_payment, timeslots, date, barcode, range_slider. A `stripe_payment` takes a fixed `amount` (major units) or priced `items` [{ id, label, unit_amount, quantity, min_quantity, max_quantity }] - the respondent only picks quantities and the server calculates the total. Content blocks (render-only, no submission key): heading, paragraph (statement), html, divider. A `paragraph` is a content block, not a textarea input. Welcome / ending screens use `kind` welcome / ending_screen / ending_redirect and carry copy in `config`. Ids and per-element config defaults are filled in when omitted.

Build a survey end-to-end from a single builder `document`: every question type, conditional branching logic, theme styling, and welcome/ending screens. This is the FULL authoring path - prefer it over update_survey when adding/replacing questions, logic, or styling. Requires `surveys:write`.

The `document` mirrors what the visual builder saves:
{
  "builder": { "name": "Q4 NPS", "settings": { "display_mode": "one_per_screen", "progress": "bar" } },
  "blocks": [
    { "id": "blk_welcome", "kind": "welcome", "position": 0, "config": { "headline": "Hi there", "body": "Two minutes, promise.", "button_label": "Start" } },
    { "id": "blk_nps", "kind": "question", "position": 1,
      "logic": { "rules": [ { "when": { "op": "and", "conditions": [ { "field": "score", "op": "lte", "value": 6 } ] }, "then": { "action": "goto", "target": "blk_reason" } } ], "fallback": { "action": "next" } },
      "elements": [ { "type": "nps", "name": "score", "config": { "label": "How likely are you to recommend us?" } } ] },
    { "id": "blk_reason", "kind": "question", "position": 2, "elements": [ { "type": "open_text", "name": "reason", "config": { "label": "What went wrong?", "long": true } } ] },
    { "id": "blk_end", "kind": "ending_screen", "position": 3, "config": { "headline": "Thanks!", "body": "We appreciate it." } }
  ],
  "theme_v2": { "tokens": { "color": { "primary": "#4f46e5" } } }
}

Element `type` vocabulary (input questions): open_text, multiple_choice_single, multiple_choice_multi, picture_selection, ranking, consent, file_upload, rating, nps, csat, ces, matrix, contact_info, cal, cta, timeslots, date, barcode, range_slider. Content blocks: paragraph (statement), divider. Per-block `logic` is the visual rule graph - `then.target` is a block id (goto/skip), rewritten internally to the target screen. Welcome / ending screens use `kind` welcome / ending_screen / ending_redirect and carry copy in `config`. Ids and per-element config defaults are filled in when omitted.

Build a multi-step funnel end-to-end from a single builder `document`: every screen, block, conditional branching logic, theme styling, and welcome/ending screens. This is the FULL authoring path - prefer it over update_funnel + add_screen/add_block when laying out or restyling a funnel. Requires `funnels:write` (funnels are a paid plan).

The `document` mirrors what the visual builder saves - one block per SCREEN (a step), each screen's fields/content as its `elements`:
{
  "builder": { "name": "Lead quiz", "settings": {} },
  "blocks": [
    { "id": "blk_welcome", "kind": "welcome", "position": 0, "config": { "headline": "Find your plan", "body": "60 seconds." } },
    { "id": "blk_goal", "kind": "question", "position": 1,
      "logic": { "rules": [ { "when": { "op": "and", "conditions": [ { "field": "goal", "op": "equals", "value": "pro" } ] }, "then": { "action": "goto", "target": "blk_pro" } } ], "fallback": { "action": "next" } },
      "elements": [
        { "type": "heading", "config": { "text": "What's your goal?", "level": "h2" } },
        { "type": "multiple_choice_single", "name": "goal", "config": { "label": "Goal", "options": [ { "value": "starter", "label": "Starter" }, { "value": "pro", "label": "Pro" } ] } },
        { "type": "cta", "config": { "button_text": "Continue" } }
      ] },
    { "id": "blk_pro", "kind": "question", "position": 2, "elements": [
      { "type": "open_text", "name": "email", "config": { "label": "Work email", "format": "email", "required": true } }
    ] },
    { "id": "blk_end", "kind": "ending_screen", "position": 3, "config": { "headline": "Thanks!" } }
  ],
  "theme_v2": { "tokens": { "color": { "primary": "#7c3aed" } } }
}

Scoring (optional): give a choice element's options a `score` in `config.options` (a number, or a `{ "bucket": points }` map) and add a top-level `outcomes` list of score bands: `"outcomes": [ { "key": "starter", "score_min": 0, "score_max": 4, "screen_id": "blk_end_low" }, { "key": "pro", "score_min": 5, "screen_id": "blk_end_high" } ]`. Bands are inclusive, a missing min/max is open-ended, an optional `score_bucket` scores one bucket instead of the total, and `screen_id` is the `id` of an `ending_screen` / `ending_redirect` block in the same document (omit it to keep the regular ending). Bands reading the same bucket must not overlap and keys must be unique, otherwise the save is rejected. The server computes the score on every submission and shows the matching band's ending; omit `outcomes` to leave the existing bands untouched, send `[]` to remove them.

Element `type` vocabulary (input blocks): open_text, multiple_choice_single, multiple_choice_multi, picture_selection, ranking, consent, file_upload, rating, cta, date, contact_info, cal, barcode, range_slider, stripe_payment. Content blocks: heading, paragraph, image, video, divider, spacer, logo, faq, countdown, html, booking.

Checkout and booking steps (native, server-priced): a `stripe_payment` element takes a payment inside the funnel - `config`: `currency` and either a fixed `amount` (major units) or `items`: [{ id, label, unit_amount, quantity, min_quantity, max_quantity }] (the visitor only picks quantities; the server calculates the total), `mode` payment|subscription, `interval` day|week|month|year (subscription), `checkout` embedded|hosted (a subscription always uses the hosted page), `required` (default true: the funnel cannot be submitted until the order is paid by a verified provider event). A `booking` element with `config.provider` `formspring` and `config.slug` of a booking page in the SAME workspace books a time inside the funnel (`required` makes it mandatory). Orders appear in list_orders / get_order and on the submission. Unlike forms/surveys a funnel NEVER rejects an unmapped element type - any type with no native funnel block (nps, matrix, csat, ...) degrades loss-free to an inert `html` block that preserves the original type, so styling/layout always saves. Screens stacking several inputs/advancing buttons are auto-split one-step-per-screen. Welcome / ending screens use `kind` welcome / ending_screen / ending_redirect with copy in `config`. Per-block `logic` is the visual rule graph - `then.target` is a block id (goto/skip). Ids and per-element config defaults are filled in when omitted. `theme_v2` carries the full styling envelope.
